@startuml data-preparation-swimlane
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam defaultFontSize 11

title Data Preparation Workstream (WS3) - Three-Layer Architecture
caption Total LOC: 4,341 lines across 8 primary scripts | Generated: 2026-02-22

|Layer 1: Immutable Original Data|
start
:Load Dataset Configurations;
note right
  **Dataset Configs:**
  - DIQA-5000 (5,000 images, MOS)
  - LIVE (779 images, DMOS)
  - CSIQ (866 images, DMOS)
  - SmartDoc-QA (smartphone captures)
  - DocLayNet (COCO, 11 classes)
  - TableBank (table structure)
  - FUNSD (forms)
  - SignaTR (writer IDs)
  - DIBCO (binarization GT)

  **Total**: 108,000+ images
end note

:Parse Dataset Labels;
note left
  **annotate_base_metadata.py**
  LOC: 1,235 lines (30.4%)

  **Components**:
  - Dataset configs: Lines 101-361
  - 9 label parsers: Lines 635-852
  - COCO cache optimization
  - Metadata generation

  **Datasets**:
  - DIQA: parse_diqa_labels()
  - LIVE: parse_live_labels()
  - CSIQ: parse_csiq_labels()
  - SmartDoc: parse_smartdoc_labels()
  - DocLayNet: parse_doclaynet_labels()
  - TableBank: parse_tablebank_labels()
  - FUNSD: parse_funsd_labels()
  - SignaTR: parse_signatr_labels()
  - DIBCO: parse_dibco_labels()
end note

:Generate OriginalFileMetadata;
note right
  **Schema Elements**:
  - file_id (UUID)
  - file_path, checksum_sha256
  - image_width, image_height
  - capture_method enum
  - domain_level1 enum
  - resolution_category

  **Immutability**: Write-once semantics
  **Validation**: Checksum verification
end note

:Normalize Quality Scores;
note right
  **Normalization Formulas**:
  - DIQA MOS (1-5): (5-mos)/4
  - LIVE DMOS (0-100): dmos/100
  - CSIQ DMOS (0-1): dmos
  - SmartDoc MOS (1-5): (5-mos)/4

  **Output**: All scores 0-1 (0=best)
  **Confidence**: From std dev or fixed
end note

:Store Layer 1 (Immutable);
note left
  **Storage Format**: Parquet
  **Schema Version**: 1.0.0
  **Write-Once**: Never modified
  **Provenance**: Full source tracking
end note

|Layer 2: Enrichment Data|

fork
  :Run Classical IQA (8 Detectors);
  note right
    **iqa_classical.py**
    LOC: 892 lines (21.9%)

    **Detectors**:
    1. Blur (Laplacian variance)
    2. Contrast (histogram)
    3. Noise (high-freq std dev)
    4. Skew (Hough transform)
    5. Illumination (brightness)
    6. JPEG blockiness (DCT)
    7. Binarization (Otsu)
    8. Bleed-through (double-sided)

    **Output**: 8-dim feature vector
  end note

fork again
  :Run ML IQA (Multi-Task Pipeline);
  note right
    **iqa_ml.py**
    LOC: 1,520 lines (35.0%)

    **Models**:
    - MobileNetV4-Conv-S (~3ms, 3 heads)
    - SigLIP 2 NAFlex (~50ms, 22 heads)

    **Features**:
    - Quality score predictions
    - Distortion type (multi-label)
    - Per-head confidence scores
    - Multi-task analysis

    **Output**: 12-dim feature vector

    Note: V2 architecture. V1 used ResNet-50/ResNet-18
    teacher-student; replaced by SigLIP 2 + MobileNetV4.
  end note

fork again
  :Run Layout Analysis;
  note right
    **layout_lite.py**
    LOC: 524 lines (12.9%)

    **Models**: Docling layout models
    (egret-xlarge / heron)

    **Detection**:
    - 11 DocLayNet classes
    - Bounding boxes
    - Element counts
    - Structural complexity

    **Output**: 15-dim feature vector
  end note

end fork

:Merge IQA + Layout Features;
note left
  **Combined Features**:
  - Classical IQA: 8 dims
  - ML IQA: 12 dims
  - Layout: 15 dims
  - Complexity: 10 dims

  **Total**: 45-dimensional vector
end note

:Calculate Document Quality Score (DQS);
note right
  **dqs_calculator.py**
  LOC: 170 lines (4.2%)

  **Formula**:
  DQS = (degradation_score × 0.6)
      + (structural_complexity × 0.4)

  **Range**: 0-100 (higher = better quality)
  **Use**: Pre-OCR risk assessment
end note

:Store Layer 2 (Enrichment);
note left
  **Storage Format**: Parquet
  **Versioning**: enrichment_version field
  **Evolution**: Models can be updated
  **Linked**: file_id → Layer 1
end note

|Layer 3: Training Labels|

:Load Layer 1 + Layer 2;
note right
  **build_training_labels.py**
  LOC: 590 lines (14.5%)

  **Inputs**:
  - Original labels (Layer 1)
  - Enrichment data (Layer 2)

  **Processing**:
  - Anchor score selection
  - 45-dim vector assembly
  - Training metadata generation
end note

:Select Anchor Score (Priority Algorithm);
note left
  **Priority Ranking**:
  1. HUMAN (weight 1.0)
  2. LLM_HIGH (weight 0.8, conf>0.8)
  3. LLM_MEDIUM (weight 0.5, conf 0.5-0.8)
  4. LLM_LOW (weight 0.3, conf<0.5)
  5. SYNTHETIC (weight 0.3)
  6. NONE (weight 0.0)

  **Algorithm**: Lines 208-290
  **Tie-Breaking**: Highest confidence wins
end note

:Assemble 45-Dim IQA Vector;
note right
  **DEGRADATION_INDEX** (Lines 60-114):

  **8 Groups, 45 Degradations**:
  - Blur/Focus (0-5): 6 types
  - Noise (6-12): 7 types
  - Geometric (13-18): 6 types
  - Illumination (19-25): 7 types
  - Compression (26-29): 4 types
  - Physical (30-36): 7 types
  - Text Quality (37-41): 5 types
  - Scanner (42-44): 3 types

  **Semantics**:
  - iqa_vector: [0.0, 1.0] severity
  - iqa_binary: {0, 1} presence/absence
end note

:Generate Training Metadata;
note left
  **TrainingLabels Dataclass** (Lines 145-171):

  **Fields**:
  - sample_id
  - iqa_vector (45 floats)
  - iqa_binary (45 bools)
  - anchor_score, anchor_source, anchor_weight
  - human_mos_normalized
  - llm_mos_normalized, llm_confidence
  - element_labels_json (Phase 9)
  - dataset_name, has_annotations
end note

:Compute Sample Weights;
note right
  **Weight Assignment**:
  - Based on anchor_source
  - HUMAN sources: weight 1.0
  - LLM_HIGH: weight 0.8
  - LLM_MEDIUM: weight 0.5
  - LLM_LOW / SYNTHETIC: weight 0.3

  **Use**: Loss weighting in training
end note

:Track Provenance;
note left
  **Provenance Fields**:
  - original_labels_used
  - enrichment_versions
  - anchor_selection_reason
  - merge_timestamp

  **Audit Trail**:
  Complete lineage from source
  datasets to training labels
end note

:Validate Training Labels;
note right
  **Validation**:
  - iqa_vector shape = (45,)
  - anchor_score in [0, 1] or None
  - All weights match source type
  - Provenance complete

  **Errors**: Logged and skipped
end note

:Export to Parquet;
note left
  **Output Format**: Parquet
  **Partitioning**: By dataset_name
  **Compression**: Snappy
  **Statistics**: Auto-generated

  **Ready**: For PyTorch DataLoader
end note

|Training Pipeline|

:Load Training Labels;

:Create PyTorch Dataset;
note right
  **Dataset Class**:
  - iqa_dataset.py (180 lines)
  - Loads parquet files
  - Applies transforms
  - Returns tensors

  **LOC**: Not counted in WS3
  (belongs to WS2: Model Training)
end note

:Apply Data Augmentation;

:Feed to Training Loop;

stop

